import json,pathlib,collections
R=pathlib.Path(__file__).parent;F=json.loads((R/'findings.json').read_text());C=json.loads((R/'coverage.json').read_text())
lines=['# Character data audit: U+0000–U+1FFF','','Snapshot: 2026-10-22. Report only; no mapping edits. Claude verification is coordinated by the parent task and is pending in this shard.','','## Coverage and strength of conclusion','','All 8,192 code-point positions were enumerated and all 5,126 non-null table entries were screened by Unicode identity, case relationships, decomposition, script-pattern comparison, or direct inventory review. Of those mappings, 4,814 are nonempty and 312 intentionally or unintentionally empty; 3,066 slots have no table entry. Unicode 17.0.0 identifies 5,125 mapped positions as assigned; U+0D49 is unassigned but has an empty mapping.','','This is exhaustive screening, not certification that 5,126 mappings are linguistically correct. A character table cannot recover unmarked vowels, inherent-vowel deletion, context-sensitive consonants, historical pronunciations, Thai/Lao vowel ordering, Korean syllable context, or word readings. Regional and historical alternatives have no single objectively most frequent mapping without a language/domain corpus. Proposed defaults below follow explicit standards and table consistency, not measured usage frequency.','','28 candidates are separated by confidence/type. The first 18 entries are direct wrong-letter/wrong-vowel/deletion candidates, followed by 3 casing defects, 3 scheme/context consistency candidates, 2 contextual-sign defects, 1 additional deleted-letter candidate, and 1 specialist-confirmation candidate. All need the requested Sonnet check before final parent reconciliation.','','## Per-character candidates','','| Unicode | Character | Current | Proposed | Class | Reason |','|---|---|---|---|---|---|']
for f in F:
 def cell(x):return str(x).replace('|','\\|').replace('\n',' ')
 lines.append('| '+' | '.join(map(cell,[f['codepoint'],f['char'],repr(f['current']),f['proposed'],f['category'],f['reason']]))+' |')
lines+=['','## Primary-source evidence','','Unicode identities and decompositions: [UnicodeData 17.0.0](https://www.unicode.org/Public/17.0.0/ucd/UnicodeData.txt), downloaded in this folder. Library of Congress charts are evidence of particular recognized schemes; their values are not asserted to be universal across all language uses of a shared script.','']
for url in dict.fromkeys(s for f in F for s in f['sources']):lines.append('- '+url)
lines+=['','## Rejected automatic false positives and unresolved families','','- Case mismatches for Ǝ/ǝ, Ʀ/ʀ, Ʃ/ʃ, Ʒ/ʒ, and Ʌ/ʌ can arise from mixed ASCII phonetic notation (e.g. SAMPA) and ordinary letter folding. Do not mechanically change every mismatch. These need an explicit policy for IPA versus orthographic Latin.','- Micro sign µ → u is a common unit-symbol ASCII fallback, even though NFKD equates it with Greek μ → m. This is not evidence that u is wrong.','- Greek Extended uses e/u where the basic modern Greek block uses i/y. Ancient and Modern Greek differ, and classical upsilon may use u. These are scheme mixing and normalization consistency risks; e and u are not individually impossible romanizations.','- U+1F75 ή and U+03AE ή, and U+1F7B ύ and U+03CD ύ, are canonically equivalent but have different table results. Group these with normalization behavior; do not claim every classical mapping is a linguistic error.','- Cyrillic й → y, х → h, ц → c; Indic c/ch, ss, uppercase R/L, rr/ll/lll; and alternate Armenian/Georgian consonant conventions can all be legitimate transliteration choices. They are not automatically mistakes merely because another standard prefers j/kh/ts or ch/sh.','- Kannada U+0CDE has formal name FA but represents the historical LLLA sound in relevant usage; its lll mapping is not convicted from its formal name. The misleading Assamese name U+09F1 was independently resolved using Unicode prose.','- Empty U+0627 alif/U+05D0 alef can be legitimate as supports/silent letters, but unconditional dropping loses written vowels in other contexts. Empty hard/soft signs and cantillation are also legitimate lossy policy choices.','- Fixed Arabic shadda W and Gurmukhi addak H cannot implement gemination. Their proposed operation requires preceding/following context; replacing each with one Latin letter cannot fully fix them.','- Several archaic Hangul jamo letters are mapped to empty: U+1120, U+113C–U+113F, U+1147, U+114E–U+1151, U+1154–U+1155, U+11EE. They are coverage/deletion gaps requiring an Old Korean scheme; they are not the same as legitimate silent initial ieung U+110B or filler deletion.','- Hebrew base letters bet/kaf/pe/shin need dagesh/sin-dot context, and unpointed words require vowel knowledge. The base p/k/b/sh mappings do not establish that every word is correct or incorrect.','- No native-specialist review of every Syriac, Thaana, Ethiopic, Cherokee, Canadian syllabic, Ogham, Runic, Khmer, Mongolian, or historic character was obtained. Full inventory screening found no additional primary-source-confirmed wrong mapping in those families during this shard.','','## Missing coverage','','The separate missing-assigned.json enumerates every assigned code point with a null/absent slot in this range. These are coverage gaps, not accusations against existing values. Entire modern blocks are absent, and even otherwise-covered blocks have missing ordinary letters (for example Ethiopic U+12A2). Do not silently count null entries as correct.','','| Block | Mapped | Empty | Assigned missing | Assigned letters missing |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
for b in C['blocks']:lines.append(f"| {b['block']} ({b['range']}) | {b['mapped']} | {b['empty']} | {b['missing_assigned']} | {b['missing_assigned_letters']} |")
lines+=['','## Reproduce','','From the repo root: `python3 research/2026-10-22-character-audit/alphabetic/audit.py`, then `build_findings.py`, then `build_report.py`. `audit.py` requires the pinned UnicodeData.txt and Blocks.txt saved in this folder. Its Python unicodedata case/decomposition checks use the interpreter UCD; coverage names/categories use pinned UCD 17.0.0. Raw 10 case anomalies and 187 decomposition anomalies remain available for independent review. No mappings were changed.']
(R/'report.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n')
